# Netlify redirects — copied verbatim into out/ by the static export, so they
# apply to every deploy (the GitHub Action uploads out/ alone and never reads
# netlify.toml). Netlify does NOT redirect a path that resolves to a file unless
# the rule is forced (`!`), and out/index.html exists, so `/` needs the force.
#
# The bare root lives at /en. Answering at the edge means the browser never
# downloads the root page at all — no HTML, no CSS, no JS, no flash.
# 302 (not 301) on purpose: browsers cache a 301 indefinitely, which would pin
# every visitor to /en if the root ever gains locale detection.
/  /en  302!
